# A named body that is never executed keeps its free names unresolved
# (docs/LMX_semantics.en.md#construction: "free names may resolve later"):
# y reads z, which nothing in the program binds, and nothing calls y. Defining y
# executes nothing and requires no source of z; make runs and returns 7, which
# the root says. Entry 7.
fn: make () int
    y: z + 1
    return: 7
end: make

int: got make()
c.printf: "MADE %d\n" got
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: got; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
